Z||000003||voyagerspe||11-14-2001||10:25 PM||||all the 125s that ive come across have been the same (exterior).  I have a 92 125 out of a grandprix  that im installing in my v8 formula .||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||11-14-2001||10:41 PM||||Alex,<P>Don't know about the length. Hard to tell, still in the car. But on both my auto Formula and my Formula "donor", the right side axles look exactly like your *old* one, based on the shape of the boots over the CV joint. <BR>If anything, I would think the Citation or Omega axles would be <I>shorter</I> than ours. The FWD minivan is supposed to have the same track width as the Fiero. Seems like the 6000 with light duty brakes also uses the same axles as the Fiero, but I'm not sure. I think the 6000 is the same car as the Citation. Now <I>I'm</I> confused   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <P>Me thinks they are confused, as well. <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||ITB 2M4||11-14-2001||11:20 PM||||The Citation is an X body, the 6000 is an A body.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jim Jimenez||11-15-2001||12:12 AM||||your axels are the same as A body axels, ie<BR>6000, Celebrity, Century, with JA1 light duty brakes,and MD9 (125) trans. X car shafts are too short.<P>that is why if you convert to a ME9 od trans, you have to use the same application and change the trans type. They are rare in production, but do not seem to be a problem with the rebuilders||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||11-15-2001||09:27 AM||||Ok, so seems these guys sent me an X body axle instead of the A body. I'll call them again. They made me pay the difference in 2nd day shipping because they say was not their error. Yeah right. I need it to be here tomorrow to put the car back on the road. Thanks all for the info  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||11-15-2001||12:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ITB 2M4:<BR><B>The Citation is an X body, the 6000 is an A body.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>DOH! <BR>Of course, you're right. Was thinking about the Celebrity and the 6000 being the same.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
